### maintainer/evals/metric-definitions.yaml  [code]
+ schema_version: 5.0.0
+ measurement_policy:
+   - Compare any baseline and candidate only with the same input fingerprint, repository ref, model, settings, and repetition count.
+   - A missing P0 obligation, P0 invention, or silent compliance truncation blocks release regardless of aggregate score.
+   - Token reduction is measured per accepted acceptance path, not per document.
+   - Experience timing starts at the user request and includes clarification, artifact generation, gate diagnosis and repair; CLI runtime alone is not end-to-end speed.
+   - Human rating claims require real user feedback tied to a version, task shape and evidence reference; agent self-rating is not user feedback.
+   - Exploratory single runs may guide iteration but cannot support a general improvement claim.
+ trace_release_proxy:
+   purpose: Local packaging review aligned to SkillHub TRACE; it is not the platform algorithm and must not predict or guarantee a public rating.
+   public_reference: https://skillhub.cn/tutorials#trace-evaluation
+   verified_on: 2026-08-12
+   scale: evidence_status_not_numeric_platform_score
+   dimensions:
+     trust:
+       meaning: security, privacy, provenance, least authority and claim honesty
+       local_evidence: [privacy_scan, package_allowlist, evidence_level_boundary, public_claim_validation]
+     reliability:
+       meaning: deterministic execution, controlled failures, dependency clarity and reproducibility
+       local_evidence: [cross_platform_tests, clean_install_smoke, runtime_budget, controlled_failure_regressions]
+     adaptability:
+       meaning: correct trigger and bounded behavior across language, task size, lifecycle stage and brownfield/greenfield shapes
+       local_evidence: [trigger_recall, trigger_precision, bilingual_paths, shape_coverage, overinterpretation_rate]
+     convention:
+       meaning: discoverable metadata, concise entry, progressive disclosure, valid package structure and no debug/private residue
+       local_evidence: [skill_creator_validation, readme_budget, runtime_manifest, package_hygiene]
+     effectiveness:
+       meaning: controlled Skill-on versus Skill-off improvement in accepted outcomes relative to token, time and rework cost
+       local_evidence: [paired_trials, p0_contract_adherence_rate, spec_rework_rate, tokens_per_accepted_ac, human_rating_evidence]
+   hard_blocks:
+     - known privacy or security leak
+     - missing or invented P0 contract
+     - unsupported public quality or acceptance claim
+     - package cannot install or execute its documented minimum path
+   honesty_rules:
+     - A local TRACE proxy PASS is not a SkillHub score.
+     - Private calibration may be reported only as anonymized aggregates; raw customer or project artifacts are never packaged.
+     - A rating target such as 4.9 is an aspiration, not evidence.
+ metrics:
+   skill_trigger_recall:
+     formula: matched requirement tasks that invoke the skill / all matched requirement tasks
+     direction: higher_is_better
+     direction: higher_is_better
+     direction: higher_is_better
+     direction: higher_is_better
+     direction: higher_is_better
